## Routing Rules

- If `ranked_actions` has entries, lead with the first action, its reason, and
  the cited signal summaries.
- Use `money_path` when the next move depends on customer progress, offer,
  proof, CTA, channel, push, playbook, page readiness, or outcome feedback.
  Keep the language evidence-based: legible, supported, connected,
  instrumented.
- Use `validation.file_contracts` when the next move depends on missing
  business-file shape. Route offer-shape gaps to `mb-think`, and ask before
  editing durable files.
- Use `content_strategy` when routing content strategy repair, stale
  channel/account platform-rule review, or disconnected layered files.
- If readiness is blocked or drift has errors, handle repair before output work.
- A `core_propagation` drift item means identity files changed after active
  push records were updated: re-check active pushes against the core files. An
  `uncodified_decisions` drift item means old accepted decisions never reached
  the reference files: route repair through `mb-think` codify mode.
- If onboarding is incomplete, use `onboarding.summary` and its checklist
  instead of inventing a setup interview.
- Use current Main Branch paths. If facts report old structural paths, follow
  the repair plan before creating new coordinated work.
- Publishing, spend, provider mutation, customer contact, migration, checkpoint
  creation, or file writes: plan first and ask for explicit approval.
- A live idea of unclear home: offers are what the business may keep selling;
  bets are time-boxed wagers; pushes are coordinated execution; proof is
  evidence; decisions explain durable changes.
- Writing to an external provider (CRM, email send, ads, account metadata) ->
  the provider-mutation contract: read-only discovery first, a sanitized plan
  (provider + object count + risk, no private rows), explicit approval,
  minimal-scope apply, verify + a private-safe record
  (docs/provider-mutation-contract.md). Reads and writes are separate surfaces.
- Commands that need a credential -> `mb connect exec <provider> -- <command>`
  (the secret stays in that command's environment; `mb connect token` refuses
  terminals and pipes). Scan agent configs for plaintext credentials with
  `mb connect hygiene`; read the recorded business identity with
  `mb connect identity`; missing providers -> `mb connect <id> --custom`.
- Surfaces below are triggered, not defaults. Lead with the business answer,
  command second; run `mb <command> --help` for flags:
  agent usage and role caps -> `mb usage --json`; whose data lives where ->
  `mb spine declare` / `mb spine show`; money flowing unattended -> `mb canary init`;
  daily read on the business -> `mb pulse init`; many repos or sites ->
  `mb fleet status` (`mb fleet refresh` first; Python 3.11+); Search Console or
  GA4 numbers -> `mb google sc query|inspect|sitemaps list` or
  `mb google ga4 report` with `--json` (not connected -> `mb connect google --oauth`);
  "show me the business" -> `mb dashboard open`; taking real money ->
  `mb production plan` (read-only); comparing lead sources ->
  `mb leads grade --file <leads.json> [--spend N]`; which creatives work ->
  `mb ledger init`; unattended or steered agent loops -> `mb automation init`;
  validating in repos with legacy debt -> `mb validate --paths <prefix>`; filing
  work without leaking private detail -> `mb issue`; an `mb` command refused or
  confused you -> `mb feedback "<what happened>" --command "<mb command name>"`
  before working around it (credential-free summary and command name only; local
  log, nothing sent); improvement ideas -> `mb suggest`; an old repo shape ->
  `mb migrate` via the doctor-recommended plan, never hand-moved files.

## Business Folders

`core/` is the business brain (offer, audience, voice, soul, proof, brand, team,
strategy, operations, finance; `core/offers/` for multi-offer repos).
`core/content-strategy.md` is the business-level content strategy; layers live in
`core/marketing/` and `core/people/`. `core/proof/` holds testimonials,
typicality, and reusable proof; use structured permission and offer-link fields,
and for proof not approved for public marketing set `permissioned_public: false`
and collect permission before public ads, pages, or claims use it.
`core/operations/spine.md` records where customer and lead data lives (`mb spine
declare` writes it, `mb spine show` reads it, doctor grades it);
`core/operations/agent-access-dossier.md` maps what agents can access, and doctor
runs only its mb-owned `mb connect test` rows. Other folders: `research/` (dated
notes), `decisions/` (dated choices), `bets/`, `pushes/` (launches, drops,
challenges, promos), `log/`, `documents/`. Weekly content planning references the
strategy files, then puts execution in `pushes/` and results in `log/`.
`mb validate` checks their frontmatter shape.

## Linking

Typed relationships live in frontmatter as repo-relative `.md` paths
(`linked_decisions:`, `linked_research:`, `linked_pushes:`, etc.); `mb graph` and
`mb validate --cross-refs` read them. Author them only from evidence in the repo
or explicit operator instruction; never invent relationships. Mirror them in a
body `## Related links` section using note-level Markdown relative links;
frontmatter wins if they disagree. If the mirror is missing or stale, preview
`mb doctor repair --plan` and ask before `mb doctor repair --apply`. Rules:
https://github.com/dmthepm/mainbranch/blob/main/docs/business-connections.md and
https://github.com/dmthepm/mainbranch/blob/main/docs/markdown-link-conventions.md.

## Connected Accounts

Never commit API keys, OAuth refresh tokens, service-account JSON, webhook
secrets, MCP tokens, or bearer tokens. Keep secrets in the runtime's local
config, an OS keychain, 1Password, `.env`, or another gitignored local file. If
a tool can spend money, publish, email, or mutate a customer account, verify it
is tethered to this repo and ask for approval before using it.

